.env*.local

# Every env file the deploy generates beside docker-compose.prod.yml.
# The builder stage runs `COPY . .` over this directory, so without these
# patterns POSTGRES_PASSWORD, BETTER_AUTH_SECRET, PAYLOAD_SECRET and the
# payment webhook secret are baked into an image layer -- readable by anyone
# who can pull the image, and contradicting the Dockerfile's own promise that
# "real secrets are injected at runtime, never baked into a layer".
# .env*.local did not cover .env.production, app.env, caddy.env or
# postgres.env.
.env.production
*.env
!.env.example
